                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any virus of the genus Hantavirus, transmitted by aerosolized rodent excreta or rodent bites, especially the deer mouse. Hantaviruses cause Hantavirus pulmonary syndrome (HPS): incubation lasts for 1–5 weeks, sickness begins with fever and muscle aches, followed by shortness of breath and coughing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "35fac5bb-5ff5-443d-90c7-406c3aab9a30",
                                                "sense_id": "c5564cc8-04b7-3ec7-a58f-a7d038fe74b9",
                                                "text": "To reveal the molecular epidemiology of hantaviruses in this region, a total of 374 small mammals (eight species of rodents and one species of shrew) were captured in the Chinese part of the Bolshoy Ussuriysky Island (Heilongjiang Province).[…] Overall, these results suggest that Bolshoy Ussuriysky Island harbors considerable hantavirus diversity."
                                            }
